ents":2,"created_at":"2025-12-05T04:08:19Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T04:26:36Z","closed_at":"2025-12-05T04:25:19Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5.1.stable, 4.3.stable \n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-12100F (8 threads) - 31.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing AUTOWRAP_WORD_SMART for autowrap_mode on a RichTextLabel doesn't wrap text properly if the text is Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, or Japanese, but only after exporting the project and running the result.\n\nIn the below example, the text is autowrapped in a way where the period character starts the newline. This is not grammatically correct in any of the aforementioned languages. The first screenshot is from running the project without exporting it. The latter screenshot is from running the exported project with Godot's default export template.\n\nRunning without exporting (correct):\n\n<img width=\"1171\" height=\"765\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e646562-04c5-4a58-b67b-d85ace5bb52f\" />\n\nRunning the exported project (incorrect):\n\n<img width=\"577\" height=\"347\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/20eb051c-7884-40b2-a9a8-1d4a0ba869fe\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNote the difference in autowrapping in the MRP after running the unexported and exported project.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[auto-wrap-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23953082/auto-wrap-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TrampolineTales","id":12213194,"n